"""Drvar: Bosnia, 25-26 May 1944.  A sample game for the Grognard engine.

At seven in the morning, on Tito's birthday, Stukas bomb the little
town of Drvar in western Bosnia, and SS paratroopers and gliders come
down on it: Operation Rösselsprung, the Knight's Move, to take the
leader of the Yugoslav Partisans dead or alive.  Tito is in a cave in
the cliff above the Unac.  Play either side against the computer, or
against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./drvar (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.drvar.json.  ./drvar --selftest checks the map and plays a
game between two computer players.
"""

